## Group knowledge base (rag-drg)

- Before writing or editing ESS inputs (ORCA, Gaussian, Q-Chem, Psi4, Molpro, PySCF), ARC input/settings
  or output parsers, or HPC submit scripts/commands, call the `rag-drg` MCP tool
  `search_knowledge` (pass `software` and `version`). Prefer `lesson`/`gotcha` results over
  your own memory. Use `lookup_level_of_theory` before translating a method between codes.
- On our clusters, programs are called by absolute path (no `module load`); take the paths,
  environment lines, queues and scratch from `server_info(<cluster>)` (`list_servers()` for the
  names). Ask these tools rather than grepping a rag_drg checkout or local ARC settings: the
  tools add the group's lessons and checks, and a local file may be out of date.
- When I correct you on any of these, call `record_lesson` (or I type `/lesson`) so the next agent does not
  repeat it: draft it, show me, record after my OK. Describe the general rule, not personal paths.
- After writing an ESS input or submit script, run `check_input` (MCP) or `rag-drg check-input`
  and fix every error before submitting. Use `render_submit_script` for cluster jobs.
- Before computing thermo with Arkane (directly or via ARC), check the sp level has Arkane AEC/BAC
  energy corrections (`search_knowledge("Arkane energy corrections", software="arkane")`); if not,
  say so and follow the fitting recipe there instead of reporting uncorrected thermo.
- When a job fails, call `diagnose_output` with the head and tail of the output file instead of
  reading the whole log.
